# Build output — generated, and `dist/` holds the emitted per-locale pages.
dist
dev-dist
coverage
node_modules

# Generated or vendored: reformatting these breaks the tool that reads them.
# `patches/` in particular is applied by `patch-package` as a byte-exact diff.
package-lock.json
patches

# Fonts and images. Prettier skips unknown extensions anyway; listed so that
# `--write .` cannot be surprised by a new asset type.
public/fonts
public/pwa

# Markdown, deliberately. The prose here is hand-wrapped at 80 columns, which
# `proseWrap: "preserve"` neither enforces nor helps with, and Prettier pads
# every table cell to the width of the widest one in its column: the audit table
# in `docs/browser-support.md` has one 350-character cell, so all five rows come
# out 393 characters wide and any edit to one cell reflows the whole table.
# Formatting is worth having where it settles arguments about code; here it just
# makes the docs harder to edit by hand.
*.md
